              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_20_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.159,
                0.329,
                0.368,
                0.346
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 6.28: A cyclic 4-gon"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.414,
            0.124,
            0.876,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The formula states that if the sides of the cyclic 4-gon have lengths "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a ,   b ,   c ,   d ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and the semi-perimeter s is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{2}(a + b + c + d)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , then: Area\u001bof "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4-\\mathrm{gen}=\\sqrt{(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)(s-d)}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.413,
            0.261,
            0.877,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It is an amazing and beautiful formula! Does it not remind us of Heron’s formula for the area of a triangle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.355,
            0.883,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can verify that the formula works out correctly in various special cases."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.394,
            0.884,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 6:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Verify Brahmagupta’s formula for the case of a rectangle. All rectangles are cyclic, so Brahmagupta’s formula should apply. Let the sides of the rectangle be a, b. Then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "s = \\frac{1}{2}(2a + 2b) = a + b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , so the formula yields:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.503,
            0.825,
            0.532
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_20_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{Area}=\\sqrt{(a+b-a)(a+b-b)(a+b-a)(a+b-b)}=\\sqrt{ab\\cdot ab}=ab,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.549,
            0.884,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "which is correct. Please check out the formula against other special cases. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 7:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Verify Brahmagupta’s formula for the case of an isosceles trapezium."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.626,
            0.461,
            0.757
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.139,
                0.626,
                0.461,
                0.757
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_20_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.171,
                0.763,
                0.429,
                0.781
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 6.29: Isosceles trapezium"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.482,
            0.621,
            0.875,
            0.72
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "All isosceles trapezia are cyclic, hence the formula should apply. The perimeter is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 a \\; + \\; 2 b \\; + \\; \\bar { 2 c } _ { \\mathrm { s } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , so "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "s = a + b + c."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Hence, the area as given by the formula should be"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.528,
            0.725,
            0.829,
            0.755
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_20_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "\\sqrt{(s - 2a)(s - 2b)(s - c)(s - c)}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.483,
            0.763,
            0.875,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "s - 2a = c + b - a, \\; s - 2b = c + a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "-2b,   s-c=a+b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the above formula simplifies to"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.241,
            0.829,
            0.754,
            0.863
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_20_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "(a+b)\\sqrt{(c+b-a)(c+a-b)}=(a+b)\\sqrt{c^2-(b-a)^2}."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
